#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:1
msgid "Add vtkAMRContourFilter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:3
msgid ""
"A vtkAMRContourFilter has been added. It computes a perfectly watertight "
"contour on vtkOverlappingAMR by creating an interface between non-refined "
"and refined grid of an AMR, interpolating data on the interface wherever "
"needed and then running contour on that interface. The result is a "
"vtkPartitionedDataSet of vtkPolyData."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:9
msgid "Assumption:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:10
msgid ""
"A single voxel in a non-refined grid is not supposed to have points in "
"common with grid of two other refinements levels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:11
msgid ""
"A single edge should not be shared between grids of more than two different "
"refinement level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:13
msgid "Implementation details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:15
msgid "Iterate over each grid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:16
msgid "If grid is of the highest refinement, just run a contour filter on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:17
msgid ""
"If not, identify the \"interface\", which are cells that are neighbors with "
"a more refined cell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:18
msgid ""
"Blank interface cells and keep a note of them, then run contour filter on "
"the non-refined grid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:19
msgid ""
"Split each interface cell into multiple unstructured cells to create an "
"actual interface between high resolution grid and low resolution grid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:20
msgid "Interpolate data on the interface wherever needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:21
msgid "Run the contour on the interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:22
msgid "Put each contour part in a partitioned dataset, this is the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:24
msgid ""
"The complex part is obviously the splitting of low resolution grid cells "
"into interface cells, The idea is to create pyramids and tetrahedrons out of "
"the cells, by adding points on the edges (from the refined grid) as well as "
"in the center of the faces and center of the voxel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:28
msgid "Iterate over each cells of the interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:29
msgid ""
"Check each edges of the cell and store the number of \"split points\", 2 "
"means not split, more mean split."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:30
msgid "Check each face of the cell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:31
msgid ""
"If no edges are split, the face is facing a non-refined grid, then create a "
"simple pyramid using the 4 face point and the voxel center."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:32
msgid ""
"If all edges are split (equally), the face is facing a refined grid, recover "
"the refined point of the refined grid and create many pyramids between these "
"quads and the voxel center."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:33
msgid ""
"Else, its an \"interface\" face, create tetrahedrons beween each \"split\" "
"edges, the face center and the voxel center."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-amr-contour-filter.md:35
msgid ""
"This creates a perfect paving of the interface, connecting the refined grid "
"with the non refined grid. The data on the interface points matters for the "
"contour. We obviously first take data from the refined grid when available, "
"then data from the non-refined grid. If no data is available (interface face "
"centers and voxel center), then a simple shepherd interpolation is used "
"using all the points on the face or the voxel respectively."
msgstr ""

